<section class="page-hero invoice-no-print">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free Invoice Generator</h1>
    <p>This <strong>free invoice generator</strong> creates a professional, itemized invoice you can download as a PDF in seconds — no signup, no watermark, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div class="invoice-no-print">
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="inv-form" onsubmit="return false;" aria-label="Invoice generator form">
        <p class="invoice-form-section-label">Your business</p>
        <div>
          <label for="inv-from-name">Business / your name</label>
          <input type="text" id="inv-from-name" placeholder="Your Company LLC" value="Your Company LLC">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="inv-from-address">Address</label>
          <textarea id="inv-from-address" rows="2" placeholder="123 Main Street&#10;City, ST 12345">123 Main Street
City, ST 12345</textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="invoice-form-row-2">
          <div>
            <label for="inv-from-email">Email</label>
            <input type="text" id="inv-from-email" placeholder="you@yourcompany.com" value="you@yourcompany.com">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="inv-from-phone">Phone (optional)</label>
            <input type="text" id="inv-from-phone" placeholder="(555) 123-4567">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="inv-logo">Logo (optional)</label>
          <input type="file" id="inv-logo" accept="image/*">
        </div>

        <p class="invoice-form-section-label">Bill to</p>
        <div>
          <label for="inv-to-name">Client name</label>
          <input type="text" id="inv-to-name" placeholder="Client Name" value="Client Name">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="inv-to-address">Client address</label>
          <textarea id="inv-to-address" rows="2" placeholder="456 Client Avenue&#10;City, ST 67890">456 Client Avenue
City, ST 67890</textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="inv-to-email">Client email (optional)</label>
          <input type="text" id="inv-to-email" placeholder="client@example.com">
        </div>

        <p class="invoice-form-section-label">Invoice details</p>
        <div class="invoice-form-row-2">
          <div>
            <label for="inv-number">Invoice #</label>
            <input type="text" id="inv-number" placeholder="INV-0001" value="INV-0001">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="inv-currency">Currency</label>
            <select id="inv-currency">
              <option value="USD">USD ($)</option>
              <option value="EUR">EUR (€)</option>
              <option value="GBP">GBP (£)</option>
              <option value="CAD">CAD ($)</option>
              <option value="AUD">AUD ($)</option>
              <option value="PKR">PKR (₨)</option>
              <option value="INR">INR (₹)</option>
              <option value="AED">AED (د.إ)</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="invoice-form-row-2">
          <div>
            <label for="inv-issue-date">Issue date</label>
            <input type="date" id="inv-issue-date">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="inv-due-date">Due date</label>
            <input type="date" id="inv-due-date">
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="invoice-form-section-label">Line items</p>
        <div class="invoice-line-header">
          <span>Description</span><span>Qty</span><span>Rate</span><span>Amount</span><span></span>
        </div>
        <div id="inv-items"></div>
        <div>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="inv-add-item">+ Add line item</button>
        </div>

        <p class="invoice-form-section-label">Totals</p>
        <div class="invoice-form-row-2">
          <div>
            <label for="inv-discount">Discount (%)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inv-discount" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" value="0">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="inv-tax">Tax (%)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inv-tax" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" value="0">
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="invoice-form-section-label">Notes / payment terms</p>
        <div>
          <textarea id="inv-notes" rows="3" placeholder="Payment due within 14 days. Bank transfer details: ...">Thank you for your business! Payment due within 14 days.</textarea>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head invoice-no-print">
        <strong>Live invoice preview</strong>
        <span id="inv-status" class="llms-status">Live</span>
      </div>

      <div id="invoice-preview" class="invoice-doc">
        <div class="invoice-doc-header">
          <div class="invoice-doc-logo" id="inv-prev-logo-wrap" hidden>
            <img id="inv-prev-logo" src="" alt="Business logo" width="140" height="70">
          </div>
          <div class="invoice-doc-from">
            <strong id="inv-prev-from-name"></strong>
            <div id="inv-prev-from-address"></div>
            <div id="inv-prev-from-email"></div>
            <div id="inv-prev-from-phone"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="invoice-doc-meta">
            <h2>INVOICE</h2>
            <div><strong>#</strong> <span id="inv-prev-number"></span></div>
            <div><strong>Issued:</strong> <span id="inv-prev-issue-date"></span></div>
            <div><strong>Due:</strong> <span id="inv-prev-due-date"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="invoice-doc-parties">
          <div>
            <h4>Bill To</h4>
            <p id="inv-prev-to-name"></p>
            <p id="inv-prev-to-address"></p>
            <p id="inv-prev-to-email"></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <table class="invoice-doc-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Description</th><th>Qty</th><th>Rate</th><th>Amount</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="inv-prev-items"></tbody>
        </table>

        <div class="invoice-doc-totals">
          <div><span>Subtotal</span><span id="inv-prev-subtotal"></span></div>
          <div id="inv-prev-discount-row" hidden><span>Discount</span><span id="inv-prev-discount"></span></div>
          <div id="inv-prev-tax-row" hidden><span>Tax</span><span id="inv-prev-tax"></span></div>
          <div class="invoice-doc-total-final"><span>Total</span><span id="inv-prev-total"></span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="invoice-doc-notes" id="inv-prev-notes"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="llms-actions invoice-no-print" style="margin-top: 18px;">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="inv-download">Download PDF</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="inv-reset">Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="llms-hint invoice-no-print">Click Download PDF to save it directly — no print dialog, no browser settings to change.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="invoice-no-print">
  <div class="container llms-explainer">

    <h2>What Should a Professional Invoice Include?</h2>
    <p>A valid, professional invoice needs a specific set of details — miss one and you risk a delayed payment while your client's accounts team asks for a corrected copy. At minimum, every invoice should have:</p>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>A unique invoice number</strong> — for your own records and your client's accounts payable system</li>
      <li><strong>Your business name, address, and contact details</strong> — so the client (and their bank) can verify who they're paying</li>
      <li><strong>The client's name and address</strong> — this is who's being billed, not necessarily who you emailed it to</li>
      <li><strong>Issue date and due date</strong> — the due date is what actually starts most companies' payment-processing clocks</li>
      <li><strong>An itemized list of what's being billed</strong> — description, quantity, rate, and line total, not just one lump sum</li>
      <li><strong>A clear total</strong>, with any tax or discount shown as its own line, not folded silently into the price</li>
      <li><strong>Payment terms or instructions</strong> — how and where to actually send the money</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to Number Your Invoices Without Creating a Bookkeeping Mess</h2>
    <p>The most common invoicing mistake isn't a missing field — it's inconsistent numbering. A sequential system (INV-0001, INV-0002...) or a date-based one (2026-09-001) both work fine; what matters is picking one and never reusing a number, even for a cancelled or voided invoice. Skipping a number is fine. Reusing one is what actually confuses your bookkeeping and your client's accounts payable system, especially once an accountant is reconciling a full year of records.</p>

    <h2>Common Invoice Mistakes That Delay Payment</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>No due date, just "payment due upon receipt"</strong> — vague terms get deprioritized behind invoices with a concrete date</li>
      <li><strong>Bundling multiple services into one line</strong> — clients querying a large lump-sum figure is one of the most common causes of payment delay</li>
      <li><strong>Missing contact information</strong> — if a question comes up and there's no direct way to reach you, the invoice sits until someone tracks you down</li>
      <li><strong>Sending the invoice from a different name or email than your business is known by</strong> — this can get flagged as suspicious by corporate finance teams and held for manual review</li>
      <li><strong>No record of what was already sent</strong> — always keep a dated copy of every invoice version you issue, especially if you correct one after the fact</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Free Invoice Generator FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>Is this invoice generator really free, with no signup?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Yes. There's no account, no email gate, and no watermark on the downloaded PDF. Fill in the form and download as many invoices as you need.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool store or send my invoice data anywhere?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Everything — your business details, client details, and line items — is generated entirely in your browser with JavaScript. Nothing is uploaded, logged, or stored on any server, including ours. Close the tab and it's gone.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I add my own logo?</summary>
        <p>Yes — use the logo upload field. It's processed locally in your browser and only appears in your invoice preview and PDF; it's never uploaded anywhere.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What file format do I get?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>A standard PDF file, generated directly in your browser and downloaded with one click — no print dialog, no settings to change, and no extra software needed.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I use this for recurring invoices?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>You can reuse the same session for multiple invoices in a row — just update the invoice number, dates, and line items between downloads. The tool doesn't save a template between visits, since nothing is stored.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it support currencies other than USD?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Yes — the currency dropdown covers USD, EUR, GBP, CAD, AUD, PKR, INR, and AED. The symbol updates throughout the preview and the totals automatically.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is an invoice from this tool legally valid?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>The format follows standard invoicing conventions used worldwide, but tax and legal requirements for invoices vary by country and business type (for example, VAT or GST registration numbers may be required in some jurisdictions). Check your local requirements, and add any mandatory fields to the notes section if needed.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I add VAT, GST, or sales tax separately from a discount?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Yes — the Tax (%) and Discount (%) fields are separate. Discount is applied to the subtotal first, then tax is calculated on the discounted amount, which matches how most invoicing software and accounting rules handle it.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will my client be able to open the PDF?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Yes — it's a standard PDF file openable in any PDF reader, browser, or email client, with no special software required on their end.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Sending invoices, but not enough new clients to send them to?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix builds the SEO and link building that brings in the clients you'll be invoicing next.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

